    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U7", "C48"],
      "pins": ["U7.4", "U7.5", "C48.1", "C48.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "/CP1_{NB}"],
      "observed": "U7.CPO (pin 4) is tied directly to +3V3. C48 is connected between +3V3 and /CP1_{NB}, which also connects to U7.CPI (pin 5); it is not connected between U7.CPO and U7.CPI.",
      "expected": "The TMC2209 charge-pump capacitor should connect between CPO and CPI, as it does for U5 and U6. U7.CPO should not be tied directly to the +3V3 rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"CPO\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"/CP1_{NB}\") ... (node (ref \"C48\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"CPI\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"C48\") (pin \"1\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"/CP0_{pH}\") ... (node (ref \"C46\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"CPO\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"37\") (name \"/CP1_{pH}\") ... (node (ref \"C46\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"CPI\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U5, U6, U7 — TMC2209 ... Stepper-motor drivers"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U7's charge-pump capacitor is miswired and its CPO pin is clamped to the 3.3 V rail. The driver may not generate the internal gate-drive supply needed to operate its motor outputs, so the corresponding pump may fail or operate incorrectly.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An unambiguous wiring error affects U7: its CPO pin is tied to +3V3, and C48 is not connected across the charge-pump pins as it is for the other two TMC2209 drivers. This is likely to prevent the Nutrient-B driver from operating correctly."
}

